  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Tuesday...\n\nWarm and breezy conditions continue today, with highs in the 70sF.\nWinds will start the day out of the west, before increasing with a\ndry cold front in the afternoon. Winds will shift to the NE\nthrough the afternoon, with gusts in the 15 to 30 mph range\n(greatest along and north of I-90 and I-94 from Livingston to\nBaker. The chance for precipitation through this afternoon is very\nlow, although a few light showers may develop later tonight and\ninto Thursday morning.\n\nA surface high moves into northeast Montana Thursday morning, \nshifting winds around to the southeast through the afternoon. \nThe latest HRRR and GFS deterministic runs show an area of \nshowers developing across locations mainly east of Billings, late \ntonight and into Friday morning. Temperatures look to cool for\nThursday with a backdoor front, as high temperatures in the 50s \nand 60sF are currently forecast.\n\nAs for total precipitation amounts from any showers over the next\n48 hours, significant moisture is not anticipated. The latest\nensembles only show a few hundredths to a tenth of an inch of\nprecipitation through Friday morning.\n\nAnother upper wave moves across on Friday, though the general\npattern trends towards ridging. Winds look to flip around once\nagain, this time to the west-north. Warmer temperatures return,\nwith highs currently forecast in the 70sF. The chance for\nprecipitation beyond Friday morning is currently low, although few\nlight showers may accompany another front and wave late Friday\ninto Saturday morning.\n\nConfidence is high that ridging will build over the Northern\nRockies over the weekend and into next week. This will bring above\nnormal temperatures and drier conditions.\n\nConfidence also remains high for warmer & drier than normal \nconditions persisting in the 8-14 day time frame (Oct 7-13), per a\nstagnant ridge over the western CONUS. The Pacific Tropics remain\nvery active and it may take a tropical storm/hurricane to alter \nthe longwave pattern at some point.\n\nMatos/JKL",
